rican History and the historic sites and national parks that hold\"}], \"fallible_prior\": [\"San Juan, Puerto Rico\"], \"prior_explanation\": \"Fort Buchanan is a United States Army post located in San Juan, Puerto Rico. No uncertainty exists regarding this fact.\", \"fallible_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0079-c5636a6f54dd:d00\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0079-c5636a6f54dd:d00:c0\", \"entity\": \"Fort Buchanan\", \"scope\": \"Location\", \"claim\": \"Fort Buchanan was a United States Army post founded in 1856 three miles southwest of present-day Sonoita in Santa Cruz County, Arizona.\", \"answer\": \"Arizona\", \"quote\": \"Fort Buchanan, Arizona Fort Buchanan was a United States Army post founded in 1856 three miles southwest of present-day Sonoita in Santa Cruz County, Arizona on the east slope of what is now called Hog Canyon.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0079-c5636a6f54dd:d02\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0079-c5636a6f54dd:d02:c0\", \"entity\": \"Fort Buchanan\", \"scope\": \"Location\", \"claim\": \"Fort Buchanan is located in Arizona, Sonoita Creek.\", \"answer\": \"Arizona, Sonoita Creek\", \"quote\": \"( United_States_Army ) dbr : File : Sonoita-Fort_Buchanan_Bridge_Ruins-1856.jpg dbp : battles dbr : Battle_of_Fort_Buchanan dbr : Apache_Wars dbp : built 1856 ( xsd : integer ) dbp : caption The ruins of Fort Buchanan in 1914 ( en ) dbp : condition dbr : Tourist_attraction dbp : imageSize 300 ( xsd : integer ) dbp : location dbr : Arizona dbr : Sonoita_Creek dbp : name Fort Buchanan ( en ) dbp : occupants United States Army ( en ) dbp : pastCommanders Michael Buckley ( en ) dbp : type U.S.\", \"original_document_number\": 3}]}"
